  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• <p>• To a medium bowl, add haloumi and cover with water to soak. <br>• Boil the kettle. Place couscous, the salt and butter in a large heatproof bowl. • Add the boiling water (3/4 cup for 2P // 1 1/2 cups for 4P) and stir to combine. Immediately cover with a plate and leave for 5 mins. Fluff up with a fork and set aside.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-1b5bd600.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Meanwhile, roughly chop tomato. <br>• Using a vegetable peeler, peel carrot into ribbons <br>• Drain and rinse chickpeas.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-4f6de110.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Drain haloumi and pat dry. Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick slices. <br>• Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium frying pan over medium-high heat. <br>• Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 mins each side. Transfer to a plate and cover to keep warm. <br>• Return the frying pan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. <br>• Cook chickpeas, tossing, until tender, 2-3 mins. <br>• Add tomato &amp; herb seasoning and tomato paste, and cook until fragrant, 1 min. <br>• Stir in the water and a pinch of brown sugar, and simmer until slightly thickened, 1 min. Season to taste.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-f6424620.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• <p>• Add tomato, carrot and salad leaves to the couscous. Add a drizzle of vinegar and olive oil. Toss to combine and season to taste. <br>• Divide veggie couscous between bowls, then top with herby chickpeas and haloumi. <br>• Crumble over fetta cubes. Dollop with yoghurt to serve.</p>",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-f8e1d030.jpeg"
    }
  ]
